    <glyph class="process" id="rx00240" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00240</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational repression</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: transcription</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: Here, we show that ETHYLENE INSENSITIVE3 (EIN3) and ETHYLENE INSENSITIVE3-LIKE1 (EIL1), two closely related Arabidopsis transcription factors previously known to regulate the ethylene pathway, negatively regulate SID2 [ICS1] expression and SA biosynthesis to repress plant immunity.</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
      <extension>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:sio="http://semanticscience.org/resource/">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="#rx00240">
