          <html:p>reaction: rx00588</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational activation</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: transcription</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: Using a transient assay, which mimics the virus infection process, we revealed that four different VSRs (p122, p38, HcPro and 2b) were also able to induce miR168. </html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
