    <glyph class="process" id="rx00716" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00716</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational repression</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: transcription</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: [...] AtERF11 binds to the promoters of ACS2 and ACS5, presumably in the DRE region, to repress its expression, resulting in decreased ethylene biosynthesis.</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
