          <html:p>reaction: rx00744</html:p>
          <html:p>type: protein activation</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: unknown</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: the brassinosteroid hormone receptor BRASSINOSTEROID INSENSITIVE 1 (BRI1) and the flagellin receptor FLAGELLIN SENSING 2 (FLS2), regulate downstream glycogen synthase kinase 3 (GSK3) and mitogen-activated protein (MAP) kinases, respectively, through phosphocoding of the BRI1-SUPPRESSOR1 (BSU1) phosphatase.</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
