    <glyph class="process" id="rx00784" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00784</html:p>
          <html:p>type: transcriptional/translational activation</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: transcription</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: Among the candidate target genes of SARD1 identified by ChIP-seq, eight genes including BAK1, BKK1, AGB1, BIK1, MEKK1, MKK4, MPK3 and CPK4 (Table 1) were previously shown to encode positive regulators of PTI. Binding of SARD1 to the promoter regions of these genes was further confirmed by ChIP-PCR (Fig. 6a).</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
      <extension>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:sio="http://semanticscience.org/resource/">
