    <glyph class="process" id="rx00925" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00925</html:p>
          <html:p>type: protein activation</html:p>
          <html:p>mechanism: binding</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: As shown in Figure 4B, we observed a clear band corresponding to COI1 in the eluate from HOP3 immunoprecipitations (IP: anti-GFP), but not in the eluates lacking HOP3, demonstrating that HOP3 also interacts with COI1 in vivo. ...However, in the presence of MeJA, JAZ10 degradation was significantly reduced to 70% in the hop3-1 mutant compared to the wild-type background (Figure 5C), demonstrating that COI1 activity is reduced in the hop3-1 mutant and highlighting the role of HOP3 in COI1 regulation.</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
      <extension>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:sio="http://semanticscience.org/resource/">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="#rx00925">
