    <glyph class="process" id="rx00943" orientation="vertical">
      <notes>
        <html:body>
          <html:p>reaction: rx00943</html:p>
          <html:p>type: translocation</html:p>
          <html:p>evidence: NRG1.1-signaling domain structure resembles the pore-forming domain of the cation channel MLKL, oligomerizes in puncta on the PM, and is sufficient to drive cytoplasmic Ca2+ influx in plants and human cells. Our data are consistent with NRG1.1 acting as a nonselective, Ca2+-permeable cation channel.</html:p>
        </html:body>
      </notes>
      <extension>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:sio="http://semanticscience.org/resource/">
            <rdf:Description rdf:about="#rx00943">
